**Caveats:** I could not visually inspect the PNGs (this model has no image input), so all counts come from the JSON reports. The OpenCV list is thresholded on a clipped display render and is dominated by small noise blobs; it must not be read as a candidate catalog. The backend's noise-normalized significance result is the stronger evidence and still classifies every hit as an **unclassified_candidate**. Differences may also reflect SPHEREx's linearly variable filters sampling slightly different wavelengths between visits. All OpenCV and significance candidates are unclassified visual aids requiring scientific validation — never confirmed detections.
